<title>USA: Marks Brothers offer priced at $22.25/shr.</title>
<headline>Marks Brothers offer priced at $22.25/shr.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marks Brothers Jewelers Inc said on Friday its 2,202,000 share public offering was priced at $22.25 per share.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be used to reduce debt, accelerate new store openings, provide working capital and for other general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>The offering consists of 1,100,000 shares offered by the company and 1,102,000 by certain selling stockholders. It was managed by Montgomery Securities and William Blair &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Marks Brothers operates 163 specialty jewelry stores.</p>
<p>	 -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
